        <mxCell id="x38" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#545B64;fontStyle=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;" value="1  Amazon Quick emits chat, feedback and agent-hours logs (message text excluded).&lt;br&gt;2  Cross-account delivery to the collector&#39;s destination in the log Region.&lt;br&gt;3  The destination writes the log files to the bucket in the collector Region.&lt;br&gt;4  Each new log file starts the log-analytics workflow (S3 event, sfn-trigger Lambda).&lt;br&gt;5  The parse step passes the records through the categorizer to the write step.&lt;br&gt;6  The write step stores them as Parquet in the same bucket.&lt;br&gt;7  Athena queries the Parquet through the Glue Data Catalog tables.&lt;br&gt;8  SPICE refreshes the datasets on a schedule.&lt;br&gt;9  The dashboard reads the SPICE datasets.&lt;br&gt;10  Viewers open the dashboard in the collector account&#39;s Quick.&lt;br&gt;11  user-sync (every 6 h) and metadata-sync (daily) assume the read-only role (ExternalId).&lt;br&gt;12  The role reads users from IAM Identity Center, and assets and SPICE metrics from Quick.&lt;br&gt;13  The read results go to the write step.&lt;br&gt;14  User and asset snapshots (JSON Lines) are written to the same bucket." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="182" width="576" x="40" y="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
