        <mxCell id="x33" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#545B64;fontStyle=0;whiteSpace=nowrap;" value="1  Amazon Quick emits the logs.&lt;br&gt;2  New &quot;local&quot; delivery from the same delivery sources.&lt;br&gt;3  The log files land in the monitored account&#39;s own bucket.&lt;br&gt;4  The log-analytics workflow turns them into Parquet.&lt;br&gt;5  Athena queries the Parquet tables.&lt;br&gt;6  SPICE refreshes the datasets.&lt;br&gt;7  The dashboard runs in the monitored account&#39;s Quick.&lt;br&gt;8  Viewers of the monitored account open it.&lt;br&gt;9  The existing cross-account delivery keeps running.&lt;br&gt;10  The collector keeps receiving its copy.&lt;br&gt;11  The collector pipeline keeps processing it.&lt;br&gt;12  The temporary dashboard stays up for comparison.&lt;br&gt;13  History is copied into the monitored bucket (Parquet only, never raw logs).&lt;br&gt;When both dashboards match: remove delivery 9 and the reader role, destroy the collector." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="182" width="534" x="40" y="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
