        <mxCell id="x33" value="1  Amazon Quick emits chat, feedback and agent-hours logs (message text excluded).&lt;br&gt;2  Same-account delivery; the delivery sources from phase 1 are reused.&lt;br&gt;3  The destination writes the log files to this account&#39;s bucket.&lt;br&gt;4  Each new log file starts the log-analytics workflow (S3 event, sfn-trigger Lambda).&lt;br&gt;5  The parse step passes the records through the categorizer to the write step.&lt;br&gt;6  The write step stores them as Parquet in the same bucket.&lt;br&gt;7  Athena queries the Parquet through the Glue Data Catalog tables.&lt;br&gt;8  SPICE refreshes the datasets on a schedule.&lt;br&gt;9  The dashboard reads the SPICE datasets.&lt;br&gt;10  Viewers open the dashboard in this account&#39;s Quick.&lt;br&gt;11  user-sync (6 h) and metadata-sync (daily) read IAM Identity Center and Quick directly.&lt;br&gt;12  The read results go to the write step.&lt;br&gt;13  User and asset snapshots (JSON Lines) are written to the same bucket.&lt;br&gt;The collector account keeps no resources and no data for this account." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#545B64;fontStyle=0;whiteSpace=nowrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="880" width="552" height="182" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
